  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nAlmost always used in the ている form ({富|と}んでいる) to describe an ongoing state of abundance. The pattern is Xに{富|と}む (to be rich in X).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {経験|けいけん}に{富|と}む — rich in experience\n- {変化|へんか}に{富|と}む — full of variety\n- {才能|さいのう}に{富|と}む — rich in talent\n- {栄養|えいよう}に{富|と}む — rich in nutrition\n- {資源|しげん}に{富|と}む — rich in resources\n\nUSAGE:\n{富|と}む is primarily used in written and formal contexts. In everyday speech, {豊|ゆた}かな is more common to express the same idea (e.g., {経験|けいけん}{豊|ゆた}かな{人|ひと}).",
